{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019TV3WZ2hMprQsR2rHg41eC","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Progress Log\n     2→\n     3→This file tracks learnings, patterns, and discoveries across Ralph Wiggum iterations.\n     4→Entries are append-only - never delete, only add.\n     5→\n     6→---\n     7→[2026-01-16] Simple Mode Verification Started\n     8→- Goal: Verify Ralph Wiggum V3 dashboard is complete and functional\n     9→- Mode: Simple (using prd.json for task tracking)\n    10→- Key files: prd.json (tasks), progress.txt (learnings), .ralph-mode (workflow mode)\n    11→- Dashboard location: ./dashboard\n    12→- Build: cd dashboard && npm run build\n    13→- Typecheck: cd dashboard && npx tsc --noEmit\n    14→- Dev server: cd dashboard && npm run dev (port 5173)\n    15→- Backend: cd dashboard && npx tsx server/index.ts (port 3001)\n    16→- Pattern: Check TypeScript compiles BEFORE marking story complete\n    17→- Pattern: Run the actual commands to verify, don't just check file existence\n    18→---\n    19→\n    20→---\n    21→[2026-01-16] US-001 - Dashboard builds without errors\n    22→- What was implemented: Verified dashboard build process\n    23→- Files checked: dashboard package.json, TypeScript config\n    24→- **Learnings:**\n    25→  - npm install shows 7 moderate vulnerabilities but doesn't block builds\n    26→  - tsc --noEmit passes cleanly with no TypeScript errors\n    27→  - Vite build produces ~500KB JS bundle (143KB gzipped)\n    28→---\n    29→\n    30→---\n    31→[2026-01-16] US-002 - Backend server starts and accepts WebSocket connections\n    32→- What was implemented: Fixed async/sync bug in database backup system\n    33→- Files changed: dashboard/server/database/backup.ts, dashboard/server/healthMonitor.ts\n    34→- **Learnings:**\n    35→  - better-sqlite3 db.backup() returns a Promise - must await before accessing the backup file\n    36→  - Server logs \"Ralph Dashboard server started\" with port info (not \"Server running on port\")\n    37→  - HealthMonitor calls DatabaseBackup.performDailyBackupIfNeeded() on startup\n    38→  - Pattern: Don't block startup on async operations - use .catch() for error handling\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→---\n    42→[2026-01-16] US-003 - Frontend dev server starts and renders\n    43→- What was verified: Vite dev server and Dashboard component\n    44→- Files checked: dashboard/vite.config.ts, dashboard/src/components/Dashboard.tsx\n    45→- **Learnings:**\n    46→  - npm run dev uses concurrently to start both Vite and backend server\n    47→  - Connection indicator is in Dashboard.tsx lines 228-240 using Badge component\n    48→  - Vite 7.3.1 with React refresh working correctly\n    49→---\n    50→\n    51→---\n    52→[2026-01-16] US-004 - Workflow mode toggle displays and functions\n    53→- What was verified: WorkflowModeToggle component and mode persistence\n    54→- Files checked: WorkflowModeToggle.tsx, Dashboard.tsx, useWebSocket.ts, server/index.ts\n    55→- **Learnings:**\n    56→  - WorkflowModeToggle uses Zap icon for Simple, Rocket icon for Advanced\n    57→  - setWorkflowMode sends WebSocket message mode:set which writes to .ralph-mode\n    58→  - mode:set handler also auto-creates missing files (prd.json, progress.txt, or IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)\n    59→---\n    60→\n    61→---\n    62→[2026-01-15] Project Initialized\n    63→- Pattern: Created complete Ralph Wiggum documentation suite\n    64→- Tip: Start with AUDIENCE_JTBD.md to ground all specs in user needs\n    65→- Tip: Use SLC releases to ship value incrementally\n    66→---\n    67→\n    68→---\n    69→[2026-01-15] Agent Installation Feature Set Complete\n    70→- Pattern: Most features in Releases 1-3 were already implemented, needed systematic verification\n    71→- Pattern: Agent installation follows the established WebSocket message pattern: add type, handler, state, UI\n    72→- Gotcha: The dashboard's npm run typecheck script doesn't exist - use `npx tsc --noEmit` instead\n    73→- Gotcha: Pre-existing lint errors in the codebase (unused vars, case block declarations) - not blockers\n    74→- Tip: YAML frontmatter in agent .md files enables name/description parsing for the UI\n    75→- Tip: No git remote configured - push will need `git remote add origin <url>` first\n    76→---\n    77→\n    78→---\n    79→[2026-01-15] Documentation Sync Complete\n    80→- Pattern: Keep tasks.json in sync with IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md when tasks are completed\n    81→- Pattern: Include all 5 releases (10 Feature Sets) in documentation for completeness\n    82→- Gotcha: tasks.json was outdated (showing 31 pending tasks) while IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md showed 63 complete\n    83→- Tip: Always verify both tracking files match before signaling ALL_TASKS_COMPLETE\n    84→- Tip: Git tags should reflect major milestones (v0.0.4 for Feature Set 10, v0.0.5 for doc sync)\n    85→---\n    86→\n    87→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"130e55cd-d481-4dd7-b33f-e0bdbfb691b6","uuid":"b652676f-e928-4096-a6a1-17322e2bdc87","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/progress.txt","content":"# Progress Log\n\nThis file tracks learnings, patterns, and discoveries across Ralph Wiggum iterations.\nEntries are append-only - never delete, only add.\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] Simple Mode Verification Started\n- Goal: Verify Ralph Wiggum V3 dashboard is complete and functional\n- Mode: Simple (using prd.json for task tracking)\n- Key files: prd.json (tasks), progress.txt (learnings), .ralph-mode (workflow mode)\n- Dashboard location: ./dashboard\n- Build: cd dashboard && npm run build\n- Typecheck: cd dashboard && npx tsc --noEmit\n- Dev server: cd dashboard && npm run dev (port 5173)\n- Backend: cd dashboard && npx tsx server/index.ts (port 3001)\n- Pattern: Check TypeScript compiles BEFORE marking story complete\n- Pattern: Run the actual commands to verify, don't just check file existence\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] US-001 - Dashboard builds without errors\n- What was implemented: Verified dashboard build process\n- Files checked: dashboard package.json, TypeScript config\n- **Learnings:**\n  - npm install shows 7 moderate vulnerabilities but doesn't block builds\n  - tsc --noEmit passes cleanly with no TypeScript errors\n  - Vite build produces ~500KB JS bundle (143KB gzipped)\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] US-002 - Backend server starts and accepts WebSocket connections\n- What was implemented: Fixed async/sync bug in database backup system\n- Files changed: dashboard/server/database/backup.ts, dashboard/server/healthMonitor.ts\n- **Learnings:**\n  - better-sqlite3 db.backup() returns a Promise - must await before accessing the backup file\n  - Server logs \"Ralph Dashboard server started\" with port info (not \"Server running on port\")\n  - HealthMonitor calls DatabaseBackup.performDailyBackupIfNeeded() on startup\n  - Pattern: Don't block startup on async operations - use .catch() for error handling\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] US-003 - Frontend dev server starts and renders\n- What was verified: Vite dev server and Dashboard component\n- Files checked: dashboard/vite.config.ts, dashboard/src/components/Dashboard.tsx\n- **Learnings:**\n  - npm run dev uses concurrently to start both Vite and backend server\n  - Connection indicator is in Dashboard.tsx lines 228-240 using Badge component\n  - Vite 7.3.1 with React refresh working correctly\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] US-004 - Workflow mode toggle displays and functions\n- What was verified: WorkflowModeToggle component and mode persistence\n- Files checked: WorkflowModeToggle.tsx, Dashboard.tsx, useWebSocket.ts, server/index.ts\n- **Learnings:**\n  - WorkflowModeToggle uses Zap icon for Simple, Rocket icon for Advanced\n  - setWorkflowMode sends WebSocket message mode:set which writes to .ralph-mode\n  - mode:set handler also auto-creates missing files (prd.json, progress.txt, or IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-15] Project Initialized\n- Pattern: Created complete Ralph Wiggum documentation suite\n- Tip: Start with AUDIENCE_JTBD.md to ground all specs in user needs\n- Tip: Use SLC releases to ship value incrementally\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-15] Agent Installation Feature Set Complete\n- Pattern: Most features in Releases 1-3 were already implemented, needed systematic verification\n- Pattern: Agent installation follows the established WebSocket message pattern: add type, handler, state, UI\n- Gotcha: The dashboard's npm run typecheck script doesn't exist - use `npx tsc --noEmit` instead\n- Gotcha: Pre-existing lint errors in the codebase (unused vars, case block declarations) - not blockers\n- Tip: YAML frontmatter in agent .md files enables name/description parsing for the UI\n- Tip: No git remote configured - push will need `git remote add origin <url>` first\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-15] Documentation Sync Complete\n- Pattern: Keep tasks.json in sync with IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md when tasks are completed\n- Pattern: Include all 5 releases (10 Feature Sets) in documentation for completeness\n- Gotcha: tasks.json was outdated (showing 31 pending tasks) while IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md showed 63 complete\n- Tip: Always verify both tracking files match before signaling ALL_TASKS_COMPLETE\n- Tip: Git tags should reflect major milestones (v0.0.4 for Feature Set 10, v0.0.5 for doc sync)\n---\n\n","numLines":87,"startLine":1,"totalLines":87}}}
