{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RimQqrKTKzEi8oAMEG3EAT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Ralph Wiggum Integration Guide\n     2→\n     3→An autonomous AI-powered development loop system that uses Claude CLI to iteratively plan and execute software development tasks.\n     4→\n     5→## What is Ralph Wiggum?\n     6→\n     7→Ralph Wiggum is an autonomous development assistant that:\n     8→\n     9→- **Plans intelligently**: Analyzes your codebase and generates detailed implementation plans\n    10→- **Executes iteratively**: Works through tasks one at a time, committing as it goes\n    11→- **Monitors in real-time**: Provides a dashboard for watching progress, logs, and git history\n    12→- **Follows your rules**: Uses project-specific coding standards and conventions\n    13→\n    14→### Key Features\n    15→\n    16→- Multiple planning modes (standard, SLC, work-scoped)\n    17→- Real-time monitoring dashboard with WebSocket updates\n    18→- Task tracking and git history visualization\n    19→- PRD and implementation plan generators\n    20→- Customizable coding rules and specialist agents\n    21→\n    22→---\n    23→\n    24→## Prerequisites\n    25→\n    26→Before integrating Ralph Wiggum, ensure you have:\n    27→\n    28→1. **Claude CLI** - Installed and authenticated\n    29→   ```bash\n    30→   # Verify installation\n    31→   claude --version\n    32→\n    33→   # If not installed, see: https://docs.anthropic.com/claude-code/\n    34→   ```\n    35→\n    36→2. **Node.js 18+** (for dashboard only)\n    37→   ```bash\n    38→   node --version  # Should be 18.x or higher\n    39→   ```\n    40→\n    41→3. **Git** (recommended)\n    42→   ```bash\n    43→   git --version\n    44→   ```\n    45→\n    46→---\n    47→\n    48→## Quick Start\n    49→\n    50→### Option A: Use the Dashboard Onboarding Wizard (Recommended)\n    51→\n    52→The dashboard includes an onboarding wizard that automatically scans your project and configures Ralph:\n    53→\n    54→1. **Copy Ralph Wiggum files to your project**\n    55→   ```bash\n    56→   cp -r /path/to/ralph-wiggum/{loop.sh,CLAUDE.md,AGENTS.md,PROMPT_*.md,dashboard} .\n    57→   chmod +x loop.sh\n    58→   ```\n    59→\n    60→2. **Start the dashboard**\n    61→   ```bash\n    62→   cd dashboard && npm install && npm run dev\n    63→   ```\n    64→\n    65→3. **Open http://localhost:5173**\n    66→   - The onboarding wizard will appear automatically\n    67→   - Click \"Scan My Project\" to detect your tech stack\n    68→   - Review and adjust the detected commands\n    69→   - Save the configuration\n    70→\n    71→4. **Run your first loop**\n    72→   ```bash\n    73→   ./loop.sh plan  # Generate implementation plan\n    74→   ```\n    75→\n    76→### Option B: Manual Setup\n    77→\n    78→#### 1. Copy Core Files\n    79→\n    80→Copy these files/directories to your project root:\n    81→\n    82→```bash\n    83→# Required files\n    84→loop.sh\n    85→CLAUDE.md\n    86→AGENTS.md\n    87→PROMPT_plan.md\n    88→PROMPT_plan_slc.md\n    89→PROMPT_plan_work.md\n    90→PROMPT_prd.md\n    91→PROMPT_analyze.md\n    92→\n    93→# Optional (for dashboard)\n    94→dashboard/\n    95→\n    96→# Optional (for coding rules)\n    97→.cursor/rules/\n    98→```\n    99→\n   100→#### 2. Configure AGENTS.md\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"130e55cd-d481-4dd7-b33f-e0bdbfb691b6","uuid":"b06da52c-d055-4ab3-8b04-f99653515ee8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/RALPH_WIGGUM_README.md","content":"# Ralph Wiggum Integration Guide\n\nAn autonomous AI-powered development loop system that uses Claude CLI to iteratively plan and execute software development tasks.\n\n## What is Ralph Wiggum?\n\nRalph Wiggum is an autonomous development assistant that:\n\n- **Plans intelligently**: Analyzes your codebase and generates detailed implementation plans\n- **Executes iteratively**: Works through tasks one at a time, committing as it goes\n- **Monitors in real-time**: Provides a dashboard for watching progress, logs, and git history\n- **Follows your rules**: Uses project-specific coding standards and conventions\n\n### Key Features\n\n- Multiple planning modes (standard, SLC, work-scoped)\n- Real-time monitoring dashboard with WebSocket updates\n- Task tracking and git history visualization\n- PRD and implementation plan generators\n- Customizable coding rules and specialist agents\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore integrating Ralph Wiggum, ensure you have:\n\n1. **Claude CLI** - Installed and authenticated\n   ```bash\n   # Verify installation\n   claude --version\n\n   # If not installed, see: https://docs.anthropic.com/claude-code/\n   ```\n\n2. **Node.js 18+** (for dashboard only)\n   ```bash\n   node --version  # Should be 18.x or higher\n   ```\n\n3. **Git** (recommended)\n   ```bash\n   git --version\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Option A: Use the Dashboard Onboarding Wizard (Recommended)\n\nThe dashboard includes an onboarding wizard that automatically scans your project and configures Ralph:\n\n1. **Copy Ralph Wiggum files to your project**\n   ```bash\n   cp -r /path/to/ralph-wiggum/{loop.sh,CLAUDE.md,AGENTS.md,PROMPT_*.md,dashboard} .\n   chmod +x loop.sh\n   ```\n\n2. **Start the dashboard**\n   ```bash\n   cd dashboard && npm install && npm run dev\n   ```\n\n3. **Open http://localhost:5173**\n   - The onboarding wizard will appear automatically\n   - Click \"Scan My Project\" to detect your tech stack\n   - Review and adjust the detected commands\n   - Save the configuration\n\n4. **Run your first loop**\n   ```bash\n   ./loop.sh plan  # Generate implementation plan\n   ```\n\n### Option B: Manual Setup\n\n#### 1. Copy Core Files\n\nCopy these files/directories to your project root:\n\n```bash\n# Required files\nloop.sh\nCLAUDE.md\nAGENTS.md\nPROMPT_plan.md\nPROMPT_plan_slc.md\nPROMPT_plan_work.md\nPROMPT_prd.md\nPROMPT_analyze.md\n\n# Optional (for dashboard)\ndashboard/\n\n# Optional (for coding rules)\n.cursor/rules/\n```\n\n#### 2. Configure AGENTS.md","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":564}}}
