unctionality\",\n   158→        \"All imports have proper type definitions\",\n   159→        \"No unused variable warnings in modified files\"\n   160→      ],\n   161→      \"priority\": 12,\n   162→      \"passes\": true,\n   163→      \"notes\": \"Verified: npx tsc --noEmit passes with no errors\"\n   164→    },\n   165→    {\n   166→      \"id\": \"US-013\",\n   167→      \"title\": \"Documentation is accurate and complete\",\n   168→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n   169→        \"RALPH_WIGGUM_README.md explains simple vs advanced modes\",\n   170→        \"AGENTS.md has correct build/test commands\",\n   171→        \"progress.txt has relevant learnings logged\",\n   172→        \"README.md exists and describes the project\"\n   173→      ],\n   174→      \"priority\": 13,\n   175→      \"passes\": false,\n   176→      \"notes\": \"Ensure documentation matches implementation\"\n   177→    },\n   178→    {\n   179→      \"id\": \"US-014\",\n   180→      \"title\": \"End-to-end verification complete\",\n   181→      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n   182→        \"Can start dashboard: cd dashboard && npm run dev\",\n   183→        \"Can switch between Simple and Advanced modes\",\n   184→        \"Can view tasks in TaskList for current mode\",\n   185→        \"Can access launcher at ?mode=launcher\",\n   186→        \"loop.sh runs and displays correct mode\",\n   187→        \"All previous stories pass\"\n   188→      ],\n   189→      \"priority\": 14,\n   190→      \"passes\": false,\n   191→      \"notes\": \"Final verification that everything works together\"\n   192→    }\n   193→  ]\n   194→}\n   195→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_us